+      "note": "ERP, payments and Slack obtain workload-exchanged tokens, and incoming bearer credentials are verified rather than forwarded. The model client's implicit credentials and database authentication provisioning are not supplied, so own-principal credential assurance for every client cannot be established."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "A01.3",
+      "result": "fails",
+      "evidence": "agent/app/identity.py:95, agent/app/identity.py:98, agent/app/identity.py:109, agent/app/main.py:155",
+      "quote": "        key = (audience, scope, ident.tenant)\n            return cached.value\n                    \"actor_token\": ident.delegated_subject,\n        delegated_subject=principal.subject,",
+      "note": "The process-wide broker caches tokens by audience, scope and tenant, omitting delegated_subject. After user A obtains a token, user B in the same tenant requesting the same audience and scope receives A's cached token without exchanging B's delegated subject. Separate RunIdentity fields therefore do not preserve the launching user's delegation on every call. External STS claim semantics are also unspecified, but the cache bypass is visible locally."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "A01.4",
+      "result": "unclear",
+      "evidence": "agent/migrations/001_init.sql:121, agent/deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:45, agent/app/identity.py:101",
